#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:1
msgid "Recipes, and the tests that freeze them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:3
msgid "What a recipe is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:5
msgid ""
"A **format** is *the specification of an operating recipe for extracting "
"information*. A **recipe** is one pair: an algorithm, and one way a "
"document writes a datum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:8
msgid ""
"That is the unit the tests freeze — not the format, and not the output "
"table. Two formats using the same recipe with different parameters need "
"**one** test between them; one format using five recipes needs **five**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:12
msgid ""
"It is also why formats are split only when their algorithms diverge, and "
"never because two documents look different."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:15
msgid "What a test of a recipe is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:17
msgid ""
"Under `tests/formats/<FORMAT>/[n/]pages/<page class>/`, three files per "
"page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "Freezes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "`<page>-pdf_blks.json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "what `pdf_extract` made of the page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "`<page>-txt_blks.json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "what `text_filter` kept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "`<page>-results.json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "what `deserialize` built"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:25
msgid ""
"`freeports-dev make-tests` writes all three. **Read what it prints before"
" confirming**: it records *what the code does now*, so confirming a wrong"
" result promotes a defect into the specification, and the test will then "
"defend it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:33
msgid ""
"Three files and not one, because a wrong result then says **which "
"segment** is wrong rather than that the page is wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:36
msgid "Which pages to freeze"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:38
msgid ""
"One per recipe, chosen for what makes it different — not the first page "
"of the class, and not a sample. A real set, from a format whose statement"
" of net assets is a matrix:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "Page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "The recipe it freezes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "37"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid ""
"sub-fund titles on one or two lines, a combined column to drop, and a "
"footnote number beside the net assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "42"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid ""
"titles on **four** lines, footnote marks in another face, and three sub-"
"funds with only the current year's column because they launched during it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:46
msgid ""
"Two pages, two recipes, and between them every shape the six pages of "
"that statement take."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:48
msgid "The `filter_data.json`, and the four conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:50
msgid ""
"For a page class whose `text_filter` needs the sub-funds an earlier step "
"found — the statement of net assets, the investment managers, the SFDR "
"annex, the ESG indicators, the renamings — the fixture needs filter data,"
" and **it is built by hand**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:54
msgid ""
"A `filter_data.json` taken as it comes produces a test that passes while "
"demonstrating nothing: if the filter recognises no fund, the deserializer"
" yields nothing and the fixture freezes the void."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:57
msgid "A useful one satisfies four conditions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:59
msgid ""
"**at least two sub-funds that pass the filter**, so the reading is "
"exercised more than once;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:60
msgid ""
"**at least one sub-fund on the page that is discarded**, so the fixture "
"proves the filter filters;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:62
msgid ""
"**the names spelled the way the earlier phases spell them.** This is the "
"condition that is easiest to get wrong and hardest to notice;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:64
msgid ""
"**for the investment managers, a residual that is not empty** — the "
"residual is the thing the algorithm actually computes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:67
msgid "Condition 3, and why it is the dangerous one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:69
msgid ""
"Sub-fund identities are compared after a deep normalisation, so case and "
"punctuation do not matter: a statement that writes `BlackRock Euro Credit"
" Enhanced Index Fund` and a schedule of investments that writes "
"`BLACKROCK EURO CREDIT ENHANCED INDEX FUND` are the same sub-fund, and a "
"fixture may use either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:74
msgid ""
"What normalisation does **not** remove is a footnote mark. `Christian "
"Equity*` and `Christian Equity` are two different sub-funds, and a mark "
"left on the name is not a blemish in one column: it is a row that quietly"
" matches nothing and disappears. The same goes for a `(continued)` the "
"running head carries, for an umbrella prefix one section writes and "
"another does not, and for a name the layout split in two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:80
msgid ""
"So the fixture's names are the **output** of the earlier phase, not what "
"you read off the page by eye."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:83
msgid "A filter data that says three things at once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:85
msgid ""
"One measured example, for a class of four SFDR annexes. The filter kept "
"there demands that the annex name a sub-fund the **holdings** named — not"
" merely one declared as a fund — so the fixture was built to exercise all"
" three outcomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "Entry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "two sub-funds with a holding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "their annexes are kept, one Article 8 and one Article 9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "one sub-fund declared as a `Fund` but with no holding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "its annex is **discarded**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md
msgid "one sub-fund absent altogether"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:95
msgid ""
"That file is worth more than three green tests: it is where the "
"difference between *declared* and *held* is written down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:98
msgid "The classes that need no filter data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:100
msgid ""
"The holdings do not. Their filter datum is the **list of companies**, "
"which the pytest plugin supplies, and a hand-written file there would "
"only pin the target list into the fixture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:103
msgid ""
"An empty `filter_data.json` is not a neutral default — it is a claim. "
"Write one only where the class needs one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:106
msgid "Freezing as the scope widens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:108
msgid ""
"The staging is: one reference page, then the whole document, then several"
" documents of the same format — and **at each step, freeze before moving "
"on**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:111
msgid ""
"Each widening is a different kind of failure. A page exercises the "
"reading of the datum, a document exercises the variation between its "
"pages, and several documents exercise what actually varies across the "
"format. An algorithm written straight against the last of the three "
"cannot tell you which of them it got wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:116
msgid ""
"The whole-document test compares against "
"`tests/formats/<FORMAT>/[n/]out/`, and the first time there is nothing to"
" compare against. Generate it deliberately, **after reading it**: from "
"then on it is the format's specification and not a snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/recipes-and-tests.md:121
msgid ""
"There is no command that regenerates a whole-document reference output. "
"`make-tests` does the per-page fixtures only. Reference outputs are not "
"rewritten as a side effect of other work — regenerate only when those "
"rows changing **is** the work, and read the diff before keeping it."
msgstr ""

